-- title:
--   Definitions for Encoding a qubit in an oscillator
-- statement:
--   The objects the formalized statements of *Encoding a qubit in an oscillator* (arXiv:quant-ph/0008040) are stated in. Each was checked against the paper by a blind read-back and a moderator.
--
--   - `cisPhase`: The source phase convention, with real phase in radians.
--   - `finiteInner`: Ordinary finite logical inner product, conjugate-linear in its first argument.
--   - `finiteWord`: Section II (17), PDF p.3: normalized finite codeword in dimension d.
--   - `finiteError`: Section II: X^a Z^b, in that order; d is positive at every use below.
--   - `finiteEncode`: Section II: encoding a logical vector by the displayed comb basis.
--   - `finiteSyndrome`: Complete half-open syndrome representatives; these are distinct from the strict central set.
--   - `finiteWindow`: Strict correction window in (16), without truncated natural-number subtraction.
--   - `finiteCodeSpace`: The finite encoder's actual subspace, in the accepted Hilbert-space convention.
--   - `finiteErrorMatrix`: Matrix of the source error X^a Z^b.
--   - `finiteErrorSpace`: Coherent span of every error in the strict central correction window.
--   - `FiniteCodeConclusion`: The full conclusion of the finite construction, including perfection and exact KL identities.
--   - `combSupportPoint`: Grid support of (27); nonzero spacing and positive n are supplied at every use.
--   - `idealComb`: The ideal encoded generalized state, as an explicitly summed Schwartz-test functional.
--   - `phasedComb`: Multiplication of a comb by a smooth phase, defined through its point masses.
--   - `rotorEncode`: Fourier coefficients of an ideal rotor codeword, with m=n*r. These bounded, periodic sequences represent distributions on the circle, not l2(Z) states.
--   - `rotorError`: Actual circle rotation followed by integer momentum translation, in Fourier coefficients.
--   - `IsRotorStabilized`: Stabilizers (19), in the integer Fourier spectrum.
--   - `rotorCell`: The strict angular/momentum window of (20), using a central representative of the angle.
--   - `wignerKernel`: Section IV (28): distributional density kernel, paired after the Wigner change of variables. This does not multiply two distributions pointwise.
--   - `wignerSign`: Sign of a Wigner lattice weight; only the odd/odd parity class is negative.
--   - `wignerQMean`: Normalized symmetric q-marginal lattice mean. Marginal pushforward is not defined for this nonnormalizable distribution; this states the source's oscillatory cancellation.
--   - `wignerPMean`: Normalized symmetric p-marginal lattice mean.
--   - `oscillatorVacuumProfile`: One-mode restriction of the pinned normalized vacuum wavefunction (source IV, PDF p.5).
--   - `coherentLatticeWave`: Ordered displacement in (29), including the BCH phase exp(i*pi*s*t). Its center is (s*alpha, 2*pi*t/alpha).
--   - `coherentStart`: A normalized coherent state with arbitrary real quadrature center.
--   - `projectedCoherent`: The ordered lattice projection of this coherent state, including the phase convention of (29).
--   - `errorCell`: Correctable open error cell of (24), with half-cell boundaries excluded.
--   - `SupportedError`: Square-integrable embedded errors with support in the correctable cell, modulo null sets.
--   - `embeddedWave`: Explicit realization of (40), with delta-comb normalization fixed by the Zak isometry. The square-root factor fixes the otherwise unspecified normalization of ideal codewords.
--   - `CellHilbert`: The physical error Hilbert space uses Lebesgue measure restricted to the open cell.
--   - `HasExactRealization`: A constructed Zak realization, with its isometry required as a conclusion.
--   - `displacedComb`: Weyl displacement exp(i*(-u*p+v*q)) of the explicit ideal comb.
--   - `IsIdealStabilized`: Common +1 eigenfunctionals of the two actual translation/modulation pullbacks.
--   - `logicalCycle`: The finite logical cyclic shift, independent of any physical syndrome.
--   - `logicalClock`: The finite logical clock, with source phase exp(+2*pi*i/n).
--   - `gkpPair`: Section VI (46), PDF p.7: sign adapter from the pinned opposite-sign form. Coordinates are grouped as alpha (p coefficient), then beta (q coefficient). The imported sigma has upper-right +I, exactly the source Omega.
--   - `schrodingerDisplacement`: Actual Schroedinger translation/modulation exp(i*sqrt(2*pi)*(alpha*p+beta*q)).
--   - `rowLattice`: Lattice generated by the rows of M, not its columns.
--   - `latticeGram`: Source (50).
--   - `IntegralMatrix`: Integral entries of a real matrix.
--   - `Unimodular`: Integer change of row basis with determinant +1 or -1.
--   - `symplecticDual`: Symplectic dual lattice, in the source's integer-pairing convention.
--   - `dualGenerator`: The particular dual basis chosen by (55)–(59).
--   - `euclideanDual`: Euclidean integer dual; used only in the CSS construction.
--   - `cssComb`: Explicit position comb on the physical CSS p-translation lattice.
--   - `HasCSSDistribution`: Nonzero common eigenfunctional for the CSS generators described in the source. The displayed source block matrix uses the generator order (q,p); its physical Weyl coordinates are adapted by swapping the two grouped coordinate blocks.
--   - `hexVector`: Two-dimensional row hexagonal lattice in (68).
--   - `planeNorm`: Euclidean plane norm, independent of the product-space max-norm instance.
--   - `hexDualVector`: Source dual lattice labels, not physical displacement coordinates.
--   - `squareDualVector`: Equal-area square dual lattice, in source label coordinates.
--   - `IsSharpRadius`: A sharp disjoint-open-ball radius, characterized by all separations and one attaining pair.
--   - `quadratureGaussianDensity`: Centered Gaussian density with standard deviation sigma in one quadrature.
--   - `squareParity`: Nearest square-lattice correction, with a fixed half-open tie convention.
--   - `squareErrorRate`: Exact odd-cell mass, including harmless translations by two logical periods.
--   - `squareJoint`: Joint logical X/Z probability induced by independent quadrature displacements.
--   - `physicalHex`: Physical dual hexagonal lattice for one encoded qubit.
--   - `hexNearest`: An actual nearest lattice point. The theorem below establishes existence for every input.
--   - `hexProbability`: Logical Pauli probabilities under nearest-lattice recovery; stabilizers are even/even labels.
--   - `SymplecticOpticalGate`: Section IX: named ideal optical operations, with mode labels and actual real parameters.
--   - `SymplecticOpticalGate.Valid`: Legal optical parameters: two different beam modes, and finite positive squeeze ratios.
--   - `realModeMixing`: Exact finite beam mixing, rather than the infinitesimal heuristic (99).
--   - `SymplecticOpticalGate.matrix`: Phase-space action of each named optical gate, in the source's grouped coordinate order.
--   - `opticalEval`: Gates are evaluated in time order.
--   - `atomEvolution`: Section XI.A: photon-number-dependent atom phase; atom=false is g, atom=true is e.
--   - `atomBranch`: The unnormalized oscillator branch after measuring the atom in the plus/minus basis.
--   - `numberSector`: Number-sector projector, kept separate from any nonnormalizable ideal comb.
--   - `paperS`: The paper's S, equal to the accepted T gate up to exp(-i*pi/8).
--   - `hadamardPlus`: Equation (112).
--   - `magicState`: Equation (114), normalized.
--   - `magicBranch`: CNOT with data control and magic-state target, followed by the indicated target outcome.
--   - `cubicLogicalPhase`: Equation (121), as a real polynomial phase.
--   - `injectionPhaseResource`: Equation (126): ideal phase-resource wavefunction; no L2 normalization is asserted.
--   - `injectionJointWave`: Product of the data wavefunction and the ideal target resource in Fig.6.
--   - `injectionInverseSum`: Position-wavefunction pullback for the data-controlled inverse SUM of Fig.6. The ket action is (q1,q2) ↦ (q1,q2-q1).
--   - `injectionPositionFiber`: Ideal target-position outcome fiber. With the unnormalizable resource this is conditional amplitude algebra, not a normalized outcome law.
--   - `phaseCorrection`: Section XI.B (125)–(127): polynomial-phase feed-forward correction.
--   - `squeezeWave`: A finite positive coordinate squeeze, with the L2 normalization retained.
--   - `cubicWave`: Cubic phase gate, on actual data wavefunctions.
--   - `ShorGate`: Actual three-qubit gates used in Fig.7; the Boolean flag chooses S inverse.
--   - `ShorGate.matrix`: Exact matrix of a gate, rather than an independent resource counter.
--   - `controlledPhaseWord`: Fig.7(a), read left to right.
--   - `inverseControlledPhaseWord`: The actual inverse of the preceding circuit.
--   - `shorWord`: Fig.7(b), with both controlled P and controlled P inverse expanded.
--   - `shorEval`: Matrix of a chronological gate list.
--   - `ccz`: Equation (153).
--   - `shorState`: The state in (150), with its actual normalized amplitudes.
--   - `shorStabilizer`: CZ on the two other wires followed by X on wire k, one of the three Shor stabilizers.
--   - `IsGaussianWave`: Normalized finite-mode pure Gaussian wavefunctions. Positivity of the real quadratic form excludes infinite squeezing, and symmetry fixes the actual quadratic coefficient.
--   - `GaussianGate`: Generators of finite affine multimode metaplectic circuits. Fourier, quadratic phases, positive squeezes, beam mixing and displacements generate the affine symplectic operations.
--   - `GaussianGate.Valid`: Infinite squeezing and coincident beam modes are excluded.
--   - `GaussianGate.act`: Actual integral/multiplier action on position wavefunctions, including exact finite mixing.
--   - `gaussianEval`: Finite, chronological composition, including mixing with other Gaussian modes.
--   - `regularFunctional`: Physical wavefunctions embedded as ordinary regular distributions.
--   - `tensorComb`: Explicit tensor product of ideal position combs, with arbitrary logical coefficients.
-- source:
--   Encoding a qubit in an oscillator, arXiv:quant-ph/0008040v3, https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0008040v3

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Defs_Gates
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Defs_QECC
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Dependency50_P10
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Frontier30_P02
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Frontier30_P10
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Next46_P16

/-!
Statements from Gottesman, Kitaev and Preskill, quant-ph/0008040v3.
Ideal combs are Schwartz-test functionals. No ambient L2 norm is assigned to them.
New definitions in this file belong to this paper; pinned coordinate, symplectic
and vacuum definitions are imported with explicit convention adapters. Compilation is pending.
-/

noncomputable section

open scoped BigOperators
open MeasureTheory Matrix ComplexConjugate
open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Dependency50.P10 (Phase sigma)

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intakenext100.P12

/-- The source phase convention, with real phase in radians. -/
def cisPhase (t : ℝ) : ℂ := Complex.exp (Complex.I * (t : ℂ))

/-- Ordinary finite logical inner product, conjugate-linear in its first argument. -/
def finiteInner {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (x y : ι → ℂ) : ℂ :=
  ∑ i, conj (x i) * y i

/-- Section II (17), PDF p.3: normalized finite codeword in dimension d. -/
def finiteWord (d r1 r2 n : ℕ) (j : Fin n) (x : ZMod d) : ℂ :=
  (Real.sqrt r2 : ℂ)⁻¹ *
    ∑ k : Fin r2, if x = ((r1 * (j.val + n * k.val) : ℕ) : ZMod d) then 1 else 0

/-- Section II: X^a Z^b, in that order; d is positive at every use below. -/
def finiteError (d : ℕ) (a b : ℤ) (x : ZMod d → ℂ) (j : ZMod d) : ℂ :=
  cisPhase (2 * Real.pi * b * (j - (a : ZMod d)).val / d) * x (j - (a : ZMod d))

/-- Section II: encoding a logical vector by the displayed comb basis. -/
def finiteEncode (d r1 r2 n : ℕ) (c : Fin n → ℂ) (x : ZMod d) : ℂ :=
  ∑ j, c j * finiteWord d r1 r2 n j x

/-- Complete half-open syndrome representatives; these are distinct from the strict central set. -/
def finiteSyndrome (d r1 r2 n : ℕ) (e : (Fin r1 × Fin r2) × Fin n) : ZMod d → ℂ :=
  finiteError d (e.1.1.val : ℤ) (e.1.2.val : ℤ) (finiteWord d r1 r2 n e.2)

/-- Strict correction window in (16), without truncated natural-number subtraction. -/
def finiteWindow (r1 r2 : ℕ) (a b : ℤ) : Prop :=
  |(a : ℝ)| < (r1 : ℝ) / 2 ∧ |(b : ℝ)| < (r2 : ℝ) / 2

/-- The finite encoder's actual subspace, in the accepted Hilbert-space convention. -/
def finiteCodeSpace (d r1 r2 n : ℕ) [NeZero d] : Submodule ℂ (EuclideanSpace ℂ (ZMod d)) :=
  Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (fun j : Fin n => WithLp.toLp 2 (finiteWord d r1 r2 n j)))

/-- Matrix of the source error X^a Z^b. -/
def finiteErrorMatrix (d : ℕ) (a b : ℤ) : Matrix (ZMod d) (ZMod d) ℂ :=
  fun x y => if x = y + (a : ZMod d) then cisPhase (2 * Real.pi * b * y.val / d) else 0

/-- Coherent span of every error in the strict central correction window. -/
def finiteErrorSpace (d r1 r2 : ℕ) [NeZero d] : Submodule ℂ (Matrix (ZMod d) (ZMod d) ℂ) :=
  Submodule.span ℂ {E | ∃ a b : ℤ, finiteWindow r1 r2 a b ∧ E = finiteErrorMatrix d a b}

/-- The full conclusion of the finite construction, including perfection and exact KL identities. -/
def FiniteCodeConclusion (d r1 r2 n : ℕ) [NeZero d] : Prop :=
  (∀ psi : ZMod d → ℂ,
    (finiteError d (r1 * n) 0 psi = psi ∧ finiteError d 0 (r2 * n) psi = psi) ↔
      ∃ c : Fin n → ℂ, finiteEncode d r1 r2 n c = psi) ∧
  (∀ c c2 : Fin n → ℂ,
    finiteInner (finiteEncode d r1 r2 n c) (finiteEncode d r1 r2 n c2) = finiteInner c c2) ∧
  QAlgorithms.Corrects (finiteCodeSpace d r1 r2 n) (finiteErrorSpace d r1 r2 : Set _) ∧
  (∀ j : Fin n,
    finiteError d (r1 * n) 0 (finiteWord d r1 r2 n j) = finiteWord d r1 r2 n j ∧
    finiteError d 0 (r2 * n) (finiteWord d r1 r2 n j) = finiteWord d r1 r2 n j) ∧
  (∀ j : Fin n,
    finiteError d r1 0 (finiteWord d r1 r2 n j) =
      finiteWord d r1 r2 n (⟨(j.val + 1) % n, Nat.mod_lt _ (Nat.zero_lt_of_lt j.isLt)⟩) ∧
    finiteError d 0 r2 (finiteWord d r1 r2 n j) =
      fun x => cisPhase (2 * Real.pi * j.val / n) * finiteWord d r1 r2 n j x) ∧
  (∀ e f : (Fin r1 × Fin r2) × Fin n,
    finiteInner (finiteSyndrome d r1 r2 n e) (finiteSyndrome d r1 r2 n f) =
      if e = f then 1 else 0) ∧
  Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (finiteSyndrome d r1 r2 n)) = ⊤ ∧
  (∀ a b a2 b2 : ℤ, finiteWindow r1 r2 a b → finiteWindow r1 r2 a2 b2 →
    ∀ c c2 : Fin n → ℂ,
    finiteInner (finiteError d a b (finiteEncode d r1 r2 n c))
      (finiteError d a2 b2 (finiteEncode d r1 r2 n c2)) =
        if (a, b) = (a2, b2) then finiteInner c c2 else 0)

/-- Grid support of (27); nonzero spacing and positive n are supplied at every use. -/
def combSupportPoint (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) (j : Fin n) (s : ℤ) : ℝ :=
  alpha * (j.val + (n : ℝ) * s)

/-- The ideal encoded generalized state, as an explicitly summed Schwartz-test functional. -/
def idealComb (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) (c : Fin n → ℂ)
    (f : SchwartzMap ℝ ℂ) : ℂ :=
  ∑ j, c j * ∑' s : ℤ, f (combSupportPoint n alpha j s)

/-- Multiplication of a comb by a smooth phase, defined through its point masses. -/
def phasedComb (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) (c : Fin n → ℂ) (phase : ℝ → ℝ)
    (f : SchwartzMap ℝ ℂ) : ℂ :=
  ∑ j, c j * ∑' s : ℤ,
    cisPhase (phase (combSupportPoint n alpha j s)) * f (combSupportPoint n alpha j s)

/-- Fourier coefficients of an ideal rotor codeword, with m=n*r. These bounded,
periodic sequences represent distributions on the circle, not l2(Z) states. -/
def rotorEncode (n r : ℕ) (c : Fin n → ℂ) (L : ℤ) : ℂ :=
  if L % (r : ℤ) = 0 then
    (Real.sqrt n : ℂ)⁻¹ * ∑ j : Fin n, c j * cisPhase (-2 * Real.pi * L * j.val / (n * r))
  else 0

/-- Actual circle rotation followed by integer momentum translation, in Fourier coefficients. -/
def rotorError (theta : ℝ) (b : ℤ) (psi : ℤ → ℂ) (L : ℤ) : ℂ :=
  cisPhase (-(L : ℝ) * theta) * psi (L - b)

/-- Stabilizers (19), in the integer Fourier spectrum. -/
def IsRotorStabilized (n r : ℕ) (psi : ℤ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  (∀ L : ℤ, psi (L - (n * r : ℕ)) = psi L) ∧
  (∀ L : ℤ, cisPhase (-2 * Real.pi * (L : ℝ) / r) * psi L = psi L)

/-- The strict angular/momentum window of (20), using a central representative of the angle. -/
def rotorCell (n r : ℕ) : Set (ℝ × ℤ) :=
  {e | |e.1| < Real.pi / (n * r) ∧ |(e.2 : ℝ)| < (r : ℝ) / 2}

/-- Section IV (28): distributional density kernel, paired after the Wigner change of variables.
This does not multiply two distributions pointwise. -/
def wignerKernel (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) (j : Fin n)
    (f : SchwartzMap (ℝ × ℝ) ℂ) : ℂ :=
  (2 * Real.pi : ℂ)⁻¹ * ∑' ab : ℤ × ℤ,
    ∫ p : ℝ,
      cisPhase (p * (combSupportPoint n alpha j ab.1 - combSupportPoint n alpha j ab.2)) *
        f ((combSupportPoint n alpha j ab.1 + combSupportPoint n alpha j ab.2) / 2, p)

/-- Sign of a Wigner lattice weight; only the odd/odd parity class is negative. -/
def wignerSign (s t : ℤ) : ℂ := if s % 2 = 1 ∧ t % 2 = 1 then -1 else 1

/-- Normalized symmetric q-marginal lattice mean. Marginal pushforward is not defined
for this nonnormalizable distribution; this states the source's oscillatory cancellation. -/
def wignerQMean (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) (j : Fin n) (M : ℕ) (f : SchwartzMap ℝ ℂ) : ℂ :=
  ((2 * (M : ℝ) + 1 : ℝ) : ℂ)⁻¹ *
    ∑ s ∈ Finset.Icc (-(M : ℤ)) (M : ℤ), ∑' t : ℤ,
      wignerSign s t * f (alpha * j.val + n * alpha * t / 2)

/-- Normalized symmetric p-marginal lattice mean. -/
def wignerPMean (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) (M : ℕ) (f : SchwartzMap ℝ ℂ) : ℂ :=
  ((2 * (M : ℝ) + 1 : ℝ) : ℂ)⁻¹ *
    ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc (-(M : ℤ)) (M : ℤ), ∑' s : ℤ,
      wignerSign s t * f (Real.pi * s / (n * alpha))

/-- One-mode restriction of the pinned normalized vacuum wavefunction (source IV, PDF p.5). -/
def oscillatorVacuumProfile (q : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Next46.P16.vacuumWave 1 (fun _ => q)

/-- Ordered displacement in (29), including the BCH phase exp(i*pi*s*t).
Its center is (s*alpha, 2*pi*t/alpha). -/
def coherentLatticeWave (alpha : ℝ) (s t : ℤ) (q : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  cisPhase (2 * Real.pi * t * q / alpha) * oscillatorVacuumProfile (q - s * alpha)

/-- A normalized coherent state with arbitrary real quadrature center. -/
def coherentStart (q0 p0 q : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  cisPhase (p0 * (q - q0 / 2)) * oscillatorVacuumProfile (q - q0)

/-- The ordered lattice projection of this coherent state, including the phase convention of (29). -/
def projectedCoherent (alpha q0 p0 : ℝ) (f : SchwartzMap ℝ ℂ) : ℂ :=
  ∑' st : ℤ × ℤ, ∫ q : ℝ,
    cisPhase (2 * Real.pi * st.2 * q / alpha) * coherentStart q0 p0 (q - st.1 * alpha) * f q

/-- Correctable open error cell of (24), with half-cell boundaries excluded. -/
def errorCell (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) : Set (ℝ × ℝ) :=
  {uv | |uv.1| < alpha / 2 ∧ |uv.2| < Real.pi / (n * alpha)}

/-- Square-integrable embedded errors with support in the correctable cell, modulo null sets. -/
def SupportedError (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) (eta : (ℝ × ℝ) → ℂ) : Prop :=
  MemLp eta 2 volume ∧ ∀ᵐ uv ∂volume, uv ∉ errorCell n alpha → eta uv = 0

/-- Explicit realization of (40), with delta-comb normalization fixed by the Zak isometry.
The square-root factor fixes the otherwise unspecified normalization of ideal codewords. -/
def embeddedWave (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) (c : Fin n → ℂ)
    (eta : (ℝ × ℝ) → ℂ) (q : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  (Real.sqrt (n * alpha / (2 * Real.pi)) : ℂ) *
    ∑ j, c j * ∑' k : ℤ,
      ∫ v : ℝ, eta (q - combSupportPoint n alpha j k, v) *
        cisPhase (v * (q + combSupportPoint n alpha j k) / 2)

/-- The physical error Hilbert space uses Lebesgue measure restricted to the open cell. -/
abbrev CellHilbert (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) :=
  Lp ℂ 2 ((volume : Measure (ℝ × ℝ)).restrict (errorCell n alpha))

/-- A constructed Zak realization, with its isometry required as a conclusion. -/
def HasExactRealization (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∃ U : (PiLp 2 (fun _ : Fin n => CellHilbert n alpha)) →ₗᵢ[ℂ]
      Lp ℂ 2 (volume : Measure ℝ),
    ∀ (c : Fin n → ℂ) (eta : CellHilbert n alpha),
      ∀ᵐ q ∂(volume : Measure ℝ),
        U (WithLp.toLp 2 (fun j => c j • eta)) q =
          embeddedWave n alpha c ((errorCell n alpha).indicator (fun uv => eta uv)) q

/-- Weyl displacement exp(i*(-u*p+v*q)) of the explicit ideal comb. -/
def displacedComb (n : ℕ) (alpha u v : ℝ) (c : Fin n → ℂ)
    (f : SchwartzMap ℝ ℂ) : ℂ :=
  ∑ j, c j * ∑' k : ℤ,
    cisPhase (v * (combSupportPoint n alpha j k + u / 2)) * f (combSupportPoint n alpha j k + u)

/-- Common +1 eigenfunctionals of the two actual translation/modulation pullbacks. -/
def IsIdealStabilized (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) (T : SchwartzMap ℝ ℂ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  (∃ D : SchwartzMap ℝ ℂ →L[ℂ] ℂ, ∀ f, D f = T f) ∧
  (∀ f g : SchwartzMap ℝ ℂ, (∀ q, g q = cisPhase (2 * Real.pi * q / alpha) * f q) → T g = T f) ∧
  (∀ f g : SchwartzMap ℝ ℂ, (∀ q, g q = f (q + n * alpha)) → T g = T f)

/-- The finite logical cyclic shift, independent of any physical syndrome. -/
def logicalCycle (n : ℕ) (c : Fin n → ℂ) (j : Fin n) : ℂ :=
  ∑ k : Fin n, if j.val = (k.val + 1) % n then c k else 0

/-- The finite logical clock, with source phase exp(+2*pi*i/n). -/
def logicalClock (n : ℕ) (c : Fin n → ℂ) (j : Fin n) : ℂ :=
  cisPhase (2 * Real.pi * j.val / n) * c j

/-- Section VI (46), PDF p.7: sign adapter from the pinned opposite-sign form.
Coordinates are grouped as alpha (p coefficient), then beta (q coefficient).
The imported sigma has upper-right +I, exactly the source Omega. -/
def gkpPair (N : ℕ) (x y : Phase N → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  -QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Frontier30.P10.symplecticPair x y

/-- Actual Schroedinger translation/modulation exp(i*sqrt(2*pi)*(alpha*p+beta*q)). -/
def schrodingerDisplacement (N : ℕ) (v : Phase N → ℝ) (psi : (Fin N → ℝ) → ℂ)
    (x : Fin N → ℝ) : ℂ :=
  cisPhase (Real.sqrt (2 * Real.pi) *
    ∑ i, v (Sum.inr i) * (x i + Real.sqrt (2 * Real.pi) * v (Sum.inl i) / 2)) *
      psi (fun i => x i + Real.sqrt (2 * Real.pi) * v (Sum.inl i))

/-- Lattice generated by the rows of M, not its columns. -/
def rowLattice {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (M : Matrix ι ι ℝ) : Set (ι → ℝ) :=
  {x | ∃ z : ι → ℤ, x = fun j => ∑ i, (z i : ℝ) * M i j}

/-- Source (50). -/
def latticeGram (N : ℕ) (M : Matrix (Phase N) (Phase N) ℝ) :=
  M * sigma N * M.transpose

/-- Integral entries of a real matrix. -/
def IntegralMatrix {ι : Type*} (A : Matrix ι ι ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ i j, ∃ k : ℤ, A i j = k

/-- Integer change of row basis with determinant +1 or -1. -/
def Unimodular {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] (R : Matrix ι ι ℤ) : Prop :=
  R.det = 1 ∨ R.det = -1

/-- Symplectic dual lattice, in the source's integer-pairing convention. -/
def symplecticDual (N : ℕ) (L : Set (Phase N → ℝ)) : Set (Phase N → ℝ) :=
  {u | ∀ v ∈ L, ∃ k : ℤ, gkpPair N u v = k}

/-- The particular dual basis chosen by (55)–(59). -/
def dualGenerator (N : ℕ) (M : Matrix (Phase N) (Phase N) ℝ) :=
  (latticeGram N M)⁻¹ * M

/-- Euclidean integer dual; used only in the CSS construction. -/
def euclideanDual {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (L : Set (ι → ℝ)) : Set (ι → ℝ) :=
  {u | ∀ v ∈ L, ∃ k : ℤ, (∑ i, u i * v i) = k}

/-- Explicit position comb on the physical CSS p-translation lattice. -/
def cssComb (N : ℕ) (Mp : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℝ)
    (f : SchwartzMap (Fin N → ℝ) ℂ) : ℂ :=
  ∑' z : Fin N → ℤ, f (fun j => Real.sqrt (2 * Real.pi) * ∑ i, (z i : ℝ) * Mp i j)

/-- Nonzero common eigenfunctional for the CSS generators described in the source.
The displayed source block matrix uses the generator order (q,p); its physical Weyl
coordinates are adapted by swapping the two grouped coordinate blocks. -/
def HasCSSDistribution (N : ℕ) (Mq Mp : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∃ T : SchwartzMap (Fin N → ℝ) ℂ →L[ℂ] ℂ, T ≠ 0 ∧
    (∀ f, T f = cssComb N Mp f) ∧
    (∀ i : Fin N, ∀ f g : SchwartzMap (Fin N → ℝ) ℂ,
      (∀ x, g x = f (fun j => x j + Real.sqrt (2 * Real.pi) * Mp i j)) → T g = T f) ∧
    (∀ i : Fin N, ∀ f g : SchwartzMap (Fin N → ℝ) ℂ,
      (∀ x, g x = cisPhase (Real.sqrt (2 * Real.pi) * ∑ j, Mq i j * x j) * f x) → T g = T f)

/-- Two-dimensional row hexagonal lattice in (68). -/
def hexVector (n : ℕ) (z : ℤ × ℤ) : ℝ × ℝ :=
  let s := Real.sqrt (2 * n / Real.sqrt 3)
  (s * (z.1 + z.2 / 2), s * Real.sqrt 3 * z.2 / 2)

/-- Euclidean plane norm, independent of the product-space max-norm instance. -/
def planeNorm (x : ℝ × ℝ) : ℝ := Real.sqrt (x.1 ^ 2 + x.2 ^ 2)

/-- Source dual lattice labels, not physical displacement coordinates. -/
def hexDualVector (n : ℕ) (z : ℤ × ℤ) : ℝ × ℝ :=
  ((hexVector n z).1 / n, (hexVector n z).2 / n)

/-- Equal-area square dual lattice, in source label coordinates. -/
def squareDualVector (n : ℕ) (z : ℤ × ℤ) : ℝ × ℝ :=
  ((z.1 : ℝ) / Real.sqrt n, (z.2 : ℝ) / Real.sqrt n)

/-- A sharp disjoint-open-ball radius, characterized by all separations and one attaining pair. -/
def IsSharpRadius (L : Set (ℝ × ℝ)) (r : ℝ) : Prop :=
  0 < r ∧ (∀ v ∈ L, ∀ w ∈ L, v ≠ w → 2 * r ≤ planeNorm (v - w)) ∧
    ∃ v ∈ L, ∃ w ∈ L, v ≠ w ∧ planeNorm (v - w) = 2 * r

/-- Centered Gaussian density with standard deviation sigma in one quadrature. -/
def quadratureGaussianDensity (sigma x : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  Real.exp (-x ^ 2 / (2 * sigma ^ 2)) / Real.sqrt (2 * Real.pi * sigma ^ 2)

/-- Nearest square-lattice correction, with a fixed half-open tie convention. -/
def squareParity (x : ℝ) : Bool :=
  decide ((Int.floor (x / Real.sqrt Real.pi + 1 / 2) : ℤ) % 2 = 1)

/-- Exact odd-cell mass, including harmless translations by two logical periods. -/
def squareErrorRate (sigma : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∫ x : ℝ, if squareParity x then quadratureGaussianDensity sigma x else 0

/-- Joint logical X/Z probability induced by independent quadrature displacements. -/
def squareJoint (sigma : ℝ) (a b : Bool) : ℝ :=
  ∫ x : ℝ, ∫ y : ℝ,
    if squareParity x = a ∧ squareParity y = b then
      quadratureGaussianDensity sigma x * quadratureGaussianDensity sigma y else 0

/-- Physical dual hexagonal lattice for one encoded qubit. -/
def physicalHex (z : ℤ × ℤ) : ℝ × ℝ :=
  (Real.sqrt (2 * Real.pi) * (hexDualVector 2 z).1,
   Real.sqrt (2 * Real.pi) * (hexDualVector 2 z).2)

/-- An actual nearest lattice point. The theorem below establishes existence for every input. -/
def hexNearest (x : ℝ × ℝ) : ℤ × ℤ :=
  Classical.epsilon (fun z => ∀ w, planeNorm (x - physicalHex z) ≤ planeNorm (x - physicalHex w))

/-- Logical Pauli probabilities under nearest-lattice recovery; stabilizers are even/even labels. -/
def hexProbability (sigma : ℝ) (a b : Fin 2) : ℝ :=
  ∫ x : ℝ × ℝ,
    if (hexNearest x).1 % 2 = (a.val : ℤ) ∧ (hexNearest x).2 % 2 = (b.val : ℤ)
      then quadratureGaussianDensity sigma x.1 * quadratureGaussianDensity sigma x.2 else 0

/-- Section IX: named ideal optical operations, with mode labels and actual real parameters. -/
inductive SymplecticOpticalGate (N : ℕ) where
  | phase (i : Fin N) (theta : ℝ)
  | beam (i j : Fin N) (theta : ℝ)
  | squeeze (i : Fin N) (ratio : ℝ)

/-- Legal optical parameters: two different beam modes, and finite positive squeeze ratios. -/
def SymplecticOpticalGate.Valid {N : ℕ} : SymplecticOpticalGate N → Prop
  | .phase _ _ => True
  | .beam i j _ => i ≠ j
  | .squeeze _ r => 0 < r

/-- Exact finite beam mixing, rather than the infinitesimal heuristic (99). -/
def realModeMixing {N : ℕ} (a b : Fin N) (theta : ℝ) : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℝ :=
  fun i j => if i = a ∧ j = a ∨ i = b ∧ j = b then Real.cos theta
    else if i = a ∧ j = b then Real.sin theta
    else if i = b ∧ j = a then -Real.sin theta
    else if i = j then 1 else 0

/-- Phase-space action of each named optical gate, in the source's grouped coordinate order. -/
def SymplecticOpticalGate.matrix {N : ℕ} : SymplecticOpticalGate N → Matrix (Phase N) (Phase N) ℝ
  | .phase k theta =>
      let A := Matrix.diagonal (fun i => if i = k then Real.cos theta else 1)
      let B := Matrix.diagonal (fun i => if i = k then Real.sin theta else 0)
      Matrix.fromBlocks A B (-B) A
  | .beam a b theta => Matrix.fromBlocks (realModeMixing a b theta) 0 0 (realModeMixing a b theta)
  | .squeeze k r => Matrix.fromBlocks
      (Matrix.diagonal (fun i => if i = k then r else 1)) 0 0
      (Matrix.diagonal (fun i => if i = k then r⁻¹ else 1))

/-- Gates are evaluated in time order. -/
def opticalEval {N : ℕ} (gates : List (SymplecticOpticalGate N)) : Matrix (Phase N) (Phase N) ℝ :=
  gates.foldl (fun A g => g.matrix * A) 1

/-- Section XI.A: photon-number-dependent atom phase; atom=false is g, atom=true is e. -/
def atomEvolution (lambda t : ℝ) (psi : ℕ × Bool → ℂ) (k : ℕ) (atom : Bool) : ℂ :=
  cisPhase (-lambda * t * k * (if atom then 1 else -1)) * psi (k, atom)

/-- The unnormalized oscillator branch after measuring the atom in the plus/minus basis. -/
def atomBranch (minus : Bool) (psi : ℕ → ℂ) (k : ℕ) : ℂ :=
  ((cisPhase (Real.pi * k / 4) + (if minus then -1 else 1) *
    cisPhase (-Real.pi * k / 4)) / 2) * psi k

/-- Number-sector projector, kept separate from any nonnormalizable ideal comb. -/
def numberSector (r : ℕ) (psi : ℕ → ℂ) (k : ℕ) : ℂ := if k % 4 = r then psi k else 0

/-- The paper's S, equal to the accepted T gate up to exp(-i*pi/8). -/
def paperS : Matrix Bool Bool ℂ := Matrix.diagonal (fun b => cisPhase (if b then Real.pi / 8 else -Real.pi / 8))

/-- Equation (112). -/
def hadamardPlus (b : Bool) : ℂ := if b then Real.sin (Real.pi / 8) else Real.cos (Real.pi / 8)

/-- Equation (114), normalized. -/
def magicState (b : Bool) : ℂ := cisPhase (if b then Real.pi / 8 else -Real.pi / 8) / (Real.sqrt 2 : ℂ)

/-- CNOT with data control and magic-state target, followed by the indicated target outcome. -/
def magicBranch (outcome : Bool) (psi : Bool → ℂ) (b : Bool) : ℂ :=
  psi b * magicState (xor outcome b)

/-- Equation (121), as a real polynomial phase. -/
def cubicLogicalPhase (alpha q : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  Real.pi / 4 * (2 * (q / alpha) ^ 3 + (q / alpha) ^ 2 - 2 * (q / alpha))

/-- Equation (126): ideal phase-resource wavefunction; no L2 normalization is asserted. -/
def injectionPhaseResource (phi : Polynomial ℝ) (q : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  cisPhase (phi.eval q)

/-- Product of the data wavefunction and the ideal target resource in Fig.6. -/
def injectionJointWave (phi : Polynomial ℝ) (psi : ℝ → ℂ) (q : ℝ × ℝ) : ℂ :=
  psi q.1 * injectionPhaseResource phi q.2

/-- Position-wavefunction pullback for the data-controlled inverse SUM of Fig.6.
The ket action is (q1,q2) ↦ (q1,q2-q1). -/
def injectionInverseSum (wave : (ℝ × ℝ) → ℂ) (q : ℝ × ℝ) : ℂ :=
  wave (q.1, q.2 + q.1)

/-- Ideal target-position outcome fiber. With the unnormalizable resource this is
conditional amplitude algebra, not a normalized outcome law. -/
def injectionPositionFiber (wave : (ℝ × ℝ) → ℂ) (a q : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  wave (q, a)

/-- Section XI.B (125)–(127): polynomial-phase feed-forward correction. -/
def phaseCorrection (phi : Polynomial ℝ) (a q : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  cisPhase (phi.eval q - phi.eval (q + a))

/-- A finite positive coordinate squeeze, with the L2 normalization retained. -/
def squeezeWave (r : ℝ) (psi : ℝ → ℂ) (q : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  (Real.sqrt r : ℂ)⁻¹ * psi (q / r)

/-- Cubic phase gate, on actual data wavefunctions. -/
def cubicWave (gamma : ℝ) (psi : ℝ → ℂ) (q : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  cisPhase (gamma * q ^ 3) * psi q

/-- Actual three-qubit gates used in Fig.7; the Boolean flag chooses S inverse. -/
inductive ShorGate where
  | phase (inverse : Bool) (target : Fin 3)
  | cx (control target : Fin 3)
  deriving DecidableEq

/-- Exact matrix of a gate, rather than an independent resource counter. -/
def ShorGate.matrix : ShorGate → Matrix (Fin 3 → Bool) (Fin 3 → Bool) ℂ
  | .phase inv t => Matrix.diagonal (fun b =>
      cisPhase ((if inv then -1 else 1) * (if b t then Real.pi / 8 else -Real.pi / 8)))
  | .cx c t => fun a b => if a = Function.update b t (xor (b t) (b c)) then 1 else 0

/-- Fig.7(a), read left to right. -/
def controlledPhaseWord (c t : Fin 3) : List ShorGate :=
  [.cx c t, .phase true t, .cx c t, .phase false c, .phase false t]

/-- The actual inverse of the preceding circuit. -/
def inverseControlledPhaseWord (c t : Fin 3) : List ShorGate :=
  [.phase true t, .phase true c, .cx c t, .phase false t, .cx c t]

/-- Fig.7(b), with both controlled P and controlled P inverse expanded. -/
def shorWord : List ShorGate :=
  [.cx 1 2] ++ inverseControlledPhaseWord 0 2 ++ [.cx 1 2] ++
    controlledPhaseWord 0 2 ++ controlledPhaseWord 0 1

/-- Matrix of a chronological gate list. -/
def shorEval (gates : List ShorGate) : Matrix (Fin 3 → Bool) (Fin 3 → Bool) ℂ :=
  gates.foldl (fun A g => g.matrix * A) 1

/-- Equation (153). -/
def ccz : Matrix (Fin 3 → Bool) (Fin 3 → Bool) ℂ :=
  Matrix.diagonal (fun b => if b 0 && b 1 && b 2 then -1 else 1)

/-- The state in (150), with its actual normalized amplitudes. -/
def shorState (b : Fin 3 → Bool) : ℂ :=
  (if b 0 && b 1 && b 2 then -1 else 1) / (Real.sqrt 8 : ℂ)

/-- CZ on the two other wires followed by X on wire k, one of the three Shor stabilizers. -/
def shorStabilizer (k : Fin 3) : Matrix (Fin 3 → Bool) (Fin 3 → Bool) ℂ :=
  fun a b => if a = Function.update b k (!(b k)) then
    (if ∀ j : Fin 3, j ≠ k → b j = true then -1 else 1) else 0

/-- Normalized finite-mode pure Gaussian wavefunctions. Positivity of the real quadratic
form excludes infinite squeezing, and symmetry fixes the actual quadratic coefficient. -/
def IsGaussianWave (N : ℕ) (psi : (Fin N → ℝ) → ℂ) : Prop :=
  (∃ (c : ℂ) (A : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ) (B : Fin N → ℂ),
    A.transpose = A ∧ c ≠ 0 ∧
    (∀ x : Fin N → ℝ, x ≠ 0 → 0 < ∑ i, ∑ j, (A i j).re * x i * x j) ∧
    ∀ x, psi x = c * Complex.exp
      (-(∑ i, ∑ j, A i j * (x i : ℂ) * x j) + ∑ i, B i * x i)) ∧
  MemLp psi 2 volume ∧ (∫ x : Fin N → ℝ, ‖psi x‖ ^ 2) = 1

/-- Generators of finite affine multimode metaplectic circuits. Fourier, quadratic phases,
positive squeezes, beam mixing and displacements generate the affine symplectic operations. -/
inductive GaussianGate (N : ℕ) where
  | fourier (mode : Fin N)
  | quadratic (B : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℝ)
  | squeeze (mode : Fin N) (r : ℝ)
  | beam (a b : Fin N) (theta : ℝ)
  | displacement (u v : Fin N → ℝ)

/-- Infinite squeezing and coincident beam modes are excluded. -/
def GaussianGate.Valid {N : ℕ} : GaussianGate N → Prop
  | .squeeze _ r => 0 < r
  | .beam a b _ => a ≠ b
  | _ => True

/-- Actual integral/multiplier action on position wavefunctions, including exact finite mixing. -/
def GaussianGate.act {N : ℕ} : GaussianGate N → ((Fin N → ℝ) → ℂ) → ((Fin N → ℝ) → ℂ)
  | .fourier k, psi => fun x => (Real.sqrt (2 * Real.pi) : ℂ)⁻¹ *
      ∫ q : ℝ, cisPhase (-(x k) * q) * psi (Function.update x k q)
  | .quadratic B, psi => fun x => cisPhase ((∑ i, ∑ j, B i j * x i * x j) / 2) * psi x
  | .squeeze k r, psi => fun x => (Real.sqrt r : ℂ)⁻¹ * psi (Function.update x k (x k / r))
  | .beam a b theta, psi => fun x => psi ((realModeMixing a b theta).transpose.mulVec x)
  | .displacement u v, psi => fun x =>
      cisPhase (∑ i, v i * (x i - u i / 2)) * psi (fun i => x i - u i)

/-- Finite, chronological composition, including mixing with other Gaussian modes. -/
def gaussianEval {N : ℕ} (gates : List (GaussianGate N)) (psi : (Fin N → ℝ) → ℂ) :
    (Fin N → ℝ) → ℂ :=
  gates.foldl (fun state g => g.act state) psi

/-- Physical wavefunctions embedded as ordinary regular distributions. -/
def regularFunctional (N : ℕ) (psi : (Fin N → ℝ) → ℂ)
    (f : SchwartzMap (Fin N → ℝ) ℂ) : ℂ := ∫ q : Fin N → ℝ, psi q * f q

/-- Explicit tensor product of ideal position combs, with arbitrary logical coefficients. -/
def tensorComb (N n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) (c : (Fin N → Fin n) → ℂ)
    (f : SchwartzMap (Fin N → ℝ) ℂ) : ℂ :=
  ∑ j : Fin N → Fin n, c j * ∑' z : Fin N → ℤ,
    f (fun i => combSupportPoint n alpha (j i) (z i))

/-- Sanity check of the scalar phase convention. -/

example : cisPhase 0 = 1 := by simp [cisPhase]

example : wignerSign 1 1 = -1 ∧ wignerSign 0 1 = 1 := by norm_num [wignerSign]

example (n : ℕ) (alpha : ℝ) : idealComb n alpha 0 = 0 := by
  funext f
  simp [idealComb]

example (psi : ℝ → ℂ) : phaseCorrection 0 3 7 * psi 7 = psi 7 := by
  simp [phaseCorrection, cisPhase]

example : opticalEval ([] : List (SymplecticOpticalGate 1)) = 1 := rfl

example : shorEval [] = 1 := rfl

example (wave : (ℝ × ℝ) → ℂ) (q : ℝ × ℝ) :
    injectionInverseSum wave q = wave (q.1, q.2 + q.1) := rfl

example (psi : ℝ → ℂ) (a : ℝ) :
    injectionPositionFiber (injectionJointWave 0 psi) a = psi := by
  funext q
  simp [injectionPositionFiber, injectionJointWave, injectionPhaseResource, cisPhase]

example (d : ℕ) (psi : ZMod d → ℂ) : finiteError d 0 0 psi = psi := by
  funext j
  simp [finiteError, cisPhase]

example (r : ℕ) (psi : ℕ → ℂ) : numberSector r (numberSector r psi) = numberSector r psi := by
  funext k
  by_cases hk : k % 4 = r <;> simp [numberSector, hk]

example : oscillatorVacuumProfile 0 = (Real.rpow Real.pi (-(1 : ℝ) / 4) : ℂ) := by
  simp [oscillatorVacuumProfile, QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Next46.P16.vacuumWave]

example (x y : Phase 0 → ℝ) : gkpPair 0 x y = 0 := by
  simp [gkpPair, QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Frontier30.P10.symplecticPair]

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intakenext100.P12


